+"""Client for the internal reports/exports API.
+
+``ApiClient`` is a thin, synchronous wrapper over an injected ``Transport``
+(see ``src.transport``). Every public method issues a single logical ``GET``
+and returns parsed domain models from ``src.models``. See README.md for the
+longer version of these notes.
+
+Requests
+    * URL is ``config.base_url`` (trailing ``/`` stripped) + the endpoint path.
+    * Query parameters whose value is ``None`` are dropped; everything else,
+      including empty strings, is sent. Values are fully percent-encoded
+      (space -> ``%20``, ``&`` -> ``%26``, ``/`` -> ``%2F``; only
+      ``A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~`` are left as-is).
+    * ``get_report`` percent-encodes the id as one path segment (``/`` included).
+      ``get_export`` inserts the id into the path *unencoded*, so only pass
+      ids that are already URL-safe.
+    * Every request sends ``Accept: application/json``,
+      ``Authorization: Bearer <config.token>`` and ``User-Agent:
+      <config.user_agent>``.
+
+Dates and times
+    * Naive ``datetime`` values are assumed to be UTC.
+    * ``list_reports`` sends ``since``/``until`` as America/Bogota local time
+      (fixed UTC-05:00) formatted ``YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`` with no offset, because
+      the reports backend has no timezone support. ``since`` is inclusive,
+      ``until`` is exclusive.
+    * ``list_exports`` sends ``created_after`` as UTC,
+      ``YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ``.
+    * Timestamps in responses (``Report.period_start``, ``Export.created_at``)
+      are returned as the raw strings the server sent, in the same conventions.
+    * Sub-second precision is truncated.
+
+Errors
+    * Any final response with status >= 400 raises ``ApiError`` carrying
+      ``status``, ``path`` (endpoint path, without base URL or query) and the
+      raw ``body``; the message includes the first 200 bytes of the body.
+    * Transport exceptions (timeouts, connection errors) and JSON/shape errors
+      from a malformed success body are not wrapped; they propagate as-is.
+
+Retries
+    * Rate limits: on HTTP 429 from any endpoint the request is resent after
+      sleeping for the ``Retry-After`` header (whole seconds, case-insensitive
+      name; missing, non-integer or negative -> 1 second), up to
+      ``config.rate_limit_retries`` (default 3) extra times.
+    * Transient 400s: only ``list_reports`` (path exactly ``/v2/reports``) is
+      retried on HTTP 400, up to ``config.retry_attempts`` (default 5) attempts
+      in total, sleeping ``retry_backoff_seconds * n`` (0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0 s by
+      default) before the n-th resend. Each attempt gets its own 429 handling.
+    * Nothing else (other 4xx, 5xx, transport errors) is retried.
+"""
 
 from __future__ import annotations
 
